    "body": "NioBay Metals President and CEO Jean-Sébastien David (L) chats with TNM Western Editor Henry Lazenby in Montreal.\nPosted By: Henry Lazenby November 19, 2026\nNioBay Metals (TSXV: NBY; US-OTC: NBYCF) plans to test material from its Crevier project in Quebec at more than 10 times the scale of its first pilot run as it seeks buyers for high-purity niobium and tantalum oxides.\nA bulk sample from Crevier, about 320 km north of Quebec City, has been crushed and bagged and is waiting for a slot at a test facility. Earlier tests yielded niobium oxide at about 99.6% purity and tantalum oxide at 99.98%.\n“So, with that, we will be able to produce more material for more clients,” President and CEO Jean-Sébastien David told The Northern Miner in Montreal early this month. “Because for now, we have nothing left, so we need to produce, produce and produce.”\nAn earlier plan for Crevier called for ferroniobium for steelmakers. NioBay is now targeting markets such as batteries, where buyers can take a year to qualify the material, David said.\nWatch the full interview with The Miner’s Western Editor, Henry Lazenby:\nPrint\nTAG: Video\nCOMMODITY: Rare Earths\nREGION: Canada\nCOMPANY: NioBay Metals\nRepublish this article",
